  "title": "Hardy-Littlewood Conjecture A (Prime k-tuples)",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $a_1, \\ldots, a_k$ be given integers. Then there exist infinitely many positive integers $n$ such that $n + a_1, \\ldots, n + a_k$ are all prime, provided that for every prime $p$, there exists an integer $m$ such that $(m + a_i, p) = 1$ for all $i$.",
